    "id": "v2-56345-p39-practice-slot-8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A landscaper mixes cement, sand and gravel in the ratio $2:3:5$. The mix contains 18 kg of sand. Find the total mass of the mix.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$60\\text{ kg}$",
      "worked": "Sand represents 3 parts.\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\text{ parts}&=18\\text{ kg}\\\\1\\text{ part}&=18\\div3=6\\text{ kg}\\\\\\text{Total parts}&=2+3+5=10\\\\10\\text{ parts}&=10\\times6=60\\text{ kg}\\end{align*}$$\nThe total mass of the mix is $60\\text{ kg}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
